' LIGHTHOUSE
' An original game by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio and
' Amy Bienvenu, 2026.
'
' You keep the light on Gull Point through five stormy nights. The lamp
' turns by clockwork, and the clockwork runs down: turn the stick round
' and round (clockwise) to wind it. Ships come in from the dark sea
' making for the harbour under the cliff. A ship knows where it is only
' while the beam has swept over it lately; one left in the dark too long
' loses its way, drifts, and can end on the reefs. From the third night
' fog banks roll in: the light cannot reach a ship in the fog, but you can
' hear its horn, and the button answers with the lighthouse's own horn,
' which guides every ship in the fog. Three wrecks, and the light has
' failed.
'
' How the beam is drawn: its rays were worked out once (scene.py): 97
' rays over the sea, each a list of cells. Every frame the old beam's
' cells get their scene tiles back and the new beam's cells get the lit
' twins (beam.asm). No sprite, no flicker, no flash.
'
' House rules kept: joystick only; text in columns 2-29 and rows 1-22;
' tiles at 128 and up; a title tune that plays once (Amy's play song ...
' once); a credits page; the frame loop is protected from the NMI and
' every screen is drawn with the NMI off after a wait.

const TSky = 128
const TStar1 = 129
const TStar2 = 130
const TSea = 131
const TSeafar = 132
const TReef = 133
const TFog = 134
const TLsky = 135
const TLstar1 = 136
const TLstar2 = 137
const TLsea = 138
const TLseafar = 139
const TLreef = 140
const TLfog = 141
const TRock = 142
const TTop = 143
const TPier = 144
const TTower00 = 145
const TTower01 = 146
const TTower10 = 147
const TTower11 = 148
const TTower20 = 149
const TTower21 = 150
const SShip = 0
const SLantern = 4
